virglrenderer: clip distances from a vertex shader to a control shader as varyings on the Mac (#692)

What: on a desktop GL without cull distances (the Mac's 4.1) a vertex shader that writes
clip distances and is followed by a tessellation control shader passes them as plain
varyings, omacvm_vclip0 (and omacvm_vclip1 for more than 4), without a location, instead of
gl_ClipDistance in its gl_PerVertex block, as virgl-shader-vs-tes-clip-varyings.patch does
before an evaluation shader without a control shader (omacvm_clipK there). Own names: the
control shader writes omacvm_clipK for its evaluation shader itself. The control shader's
key gets vs_clip_in from the vertex shader's variable info (tess_clip_out), in whole and
separable programs; it then has no gl_ClipDistance in its gl_in[] block, declares the same
omacvm_vclipK[] arrays, also when it reads none, and reads them the way the evaluation
shader reads omacvm_clipK[] (one helper, clip_varyings_in(), and the name as a parameter of
emit_tess_clip_varyings() and create_tes_clip_varyings_src()): an indirect index picks the
array at run time, a distance not passed reads 0. A control shader's reads of its own
gl_out[] are not changed. Not as the last stage, not with cull distances, nor when the
varyings would not fit (MAX_VARYING): then both keep gl_PerVertex as before. GLES and
hosts with cull distances keep their GLSL. Without a control shader nothing changes.
Why: a whole program whose vertex shader writes gl_ClipDistance[4..7] into a control
shader drew nothing on the M4's and the M1 Max's GPUs (macOS 27), with no fallback line
and no crash; the same text writing only [0..3] drew, and Apple's software renderer drew
all of it (#692, from #589). The guest's Mesa sends that whenever an app writes 5 to 8
clip distances in a loop before a control shader (the 3.2.19 gate's tcs-8*loop rows).
The same values as plain varyings draw on both GPUs.
Upstream: not sent (a workaround for Apple's GL).
Test: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c: the GLSL of a vertex shader with 1, 5 and 8
clip distances before a control shader on the Mac's config (whole and separable) has no
gl_ClipDistance, declares omacvm_vclip0 (and omacvm_vclip1), and compiles on the Mac's GL;
its control shader declares the same names and reads them, with a constant and an indirect
index; as the last stage, before an evaluation shader without a control shader, with cull
distances and on GLES the text is as before. Tests/virgl/test-whole-program-shapes.c L
rows with 5-8 distances draw on the GPU.

